.TH "RECORD\-ERRORS\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-errors\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-errors\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-errors\.sh\fR scans workflow output files for error indicators using the \fBcheck_for_errors\fR function from \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR\. It sources \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR and operates in two phases:
.P
\fBPhase 1 \(em current or recent output:\fR
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBIf \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is running\fR (the PID file exists and its stderr file descriptor resolves to a regular file), \fBcheck_for_errors\fR is run non\-interactively against the live stderr file\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBIf \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is not running\fR, the script iterates over all \fB*\.out\fR files in the current working directory and prompts the user interactively for each one:
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBY\fR \(em run \fBcheck_for_errors\fR on the file\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBN\fR \(em skip the file\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBQ\fR \(em exit the script immediately\.
.IP "" 0

.IP "" 0
.P
\fBPhase 2 \(em Slurm output:\fR
.P
Unconditionally runs \fBcheck_for_errors\fR on every \fB*\.out\fR file found under \fBslurm\-outputs/\fR, regardless of the outcome of phase 1\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. All configuration is supplied via environment variables inherited from \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on normal completion\.
.P
Returns 0 if the user enters \fBQ\fR during interactive prompting\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR validation fails at source time (see \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR documentation)\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR
The name of the workflow program being monitored\. Set and validated by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR at source time\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Used by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR to construct the PID file path\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_PID_FILE\fR
Path to the PID file, exported by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR as \fB/tmp/record\.$USER\.$RECORD_DBTYPE\.$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.pid\fR\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Scan the current workflow run or recent output files:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-errors\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR
Common library sourced at startup\. Must be present in the working directory or on \fBPATH\fR\.
.TP
\fB/tmp/record\.<USER>\.<RECORD_DBTYPE>\.<RECORD_START_PROGRAM>\.pid\fR
PID file written by the workflow run\. Read to determine whether \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is currently running\.
.TP
\fB*\.out\fR
Output files in the current working directory, inspected interactively when the program is not running\.
.TP
\fBslurm\-outputs/*\.out\fR
Slurm job output files, always scanned non\-interactively in phase 2\.
